                <pb facs="0450" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94119/690: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-22T16:00:00+09:00">November 22, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 22—7:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1181. Reference Chungking’s 578, November 20, 10 a.m., to the Department via
                    Shanghai. The Embassy has learned definitely that the United Press in Tokyo did
                    not send the despatch quoted in Chungking’s telegram under reference and further
                    that the United Press here has not sent any report containing similar
                    information.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Chungking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
